WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.120
The one piece manga just showed us EXACTLY WHY&nbsp;
the Sun God Nika’s abilities are ABSOLUTELY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:12.120
BROKEN. Because as we see at the end of this&nbsp;
chapter, Bonney revealed a completely new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.120
power that allowed her to imitate Nika’s&nbsp;
rubber fist, and, man, did it leave this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.360
miserable government agent completely knocked&nbsp;
out. And all of this has got me thinking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:28.960
if Bonney’s attack was SO POWERFUL just by&nbsp;
imitating Nika, then Luffy’s Nika abilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.040
are 100% the most game-changing abilities in&nbsp;
the story. Which of course makes sense for our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.840
main character to have, but let’s break down&nbsp;
what makes them just so ridiculously powerful.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.480
First, there’s the actual rubbery stretchy&nbsp;
abilities that everyone has discussed many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:55.280
times now, but to see it being used by someone&nbsp;
else is just absolutely mind-blowing. I mean keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:01.160
in mind that Bonney was basically just a normal&nbsp;
child. She didn’t have any special lineage or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:10.400
training that made her extra strong, so the fact&nbsp;
that this partial Nika transformation allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.560
her to take out a full-blown government agent&nbsp;
is just incredible. Beyond that though, it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:23.160
the versatility of these powers that truly makes&nbsp;
them so strong because Luffy, and now somewhat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.160 --> 00:03:12.240
for Bonney, can adapt the powers to whatever&nbsp;
they need in order to overcome the battle.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:24.600
However, there is another part of Nika’s abilities&nbsp;
that just really stood out to me which is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:30.920
power of belief. Because we’ve seen all throughout&nbsp;
the story that Luffy, and more recently Nika,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:41.320
bring hope to those who were about to give up.&nbsp;
You can think back to almost any arc in One Piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:48.600
and Luffy is the one who brought hope. But even&nbsp;
bringing this to the current backstory, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:55.160
Kuma’s belief in Nika from a young age that really&nbsp;
helped him never give up his search for freedom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:02.200
and a cure for Bonney. So it was just incredibly&nbsp;
awesome to see that when Bonney needed to escape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:08.360
from the person keeping her captive, she thought&nbsp;
of Nika and those powers helped her escape.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:13.400
Honestly though, it goes even further than&nbsp;
that because at this point I’m starting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:21.600
truly believe that Nika was basically a god&nbsp;
that the Buccaneers and even other races used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.640
to worship. If you really look into it,&nbsp;
there are signs pointing to Sun God Nika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:34.080
being a major religious figure all throughout&nbsp;
the story. If you haven’t seen these examples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:42.440
I can just point out the sun-logo that appears in&nbsp;
many places such as the cross in Kuma’s church,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.640
the fishmen sun pirate symbol, the&nbsp;
Kozuki crest, the Alabasta flag,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:54.360
and even in Skypiea. And the one thing that&nbsp;
ties all these people and places together is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.360 --> 00:05:02.280
their relationship to the Ancient Kingdom. So&nbsp;
at this point, since we know Nika was a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:09.400
figure in the Ancient Kingdom, I’m starting&nbsp;
to think Nika was truly their founder or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:14.280
a literal god that many of the Ancient&nbsp;
Kingdom allies started to worship. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:21.080
is how the Buccaneer religion started, and&nbsp;
that has somehow carried on to the very day.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:26.720
And while we’re talking about religion, it&nbsp;
is also need to bring up that I kinda wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:35.880
if Mihawk was a former Holy Knight who was&nbsp;
eventually converted to the Nika religion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:41.840
Which sounds crazy, I know, but there are a ton&nbsp;
of connections between Mihawk and Imu’s throne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.846
such as the markings on the throne being&nbsp;
very similar to the markings on Mihawk’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:05.800
sword. Plus Mihawk’s eyes are eerily similar&nbsp;
to Imu’s. But you might be wondering how all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:10.720
this makes me think that he believes in&nbsp;
Nika, and the answer to that is mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:19.000
based on his design. Because clearly he has&nbsp;
a whole Christianity vibe going on. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:23.800
his cross necklace reminds me a lot of the&nbsp;
cross that Kuma had in his church back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:33.080
the Sorbet Kingdom. And if Mihawk does believe&nbsp;
in Nika then it would explain why he let good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:45.840
pirates like Luffy and Zoro survive when&nbsp;
he so easily could have killed them all.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:56.480
Now, I just had to bring that up because man it&nbsp;
was just so cool to see Bonney’s Nika power and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:01.600
this honestly new power might be one of the MOST&nbsp;
BROKEN abilities in the entire story. Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:09.120
just by believing in this new future, Bonney&nbsp;
can literally transform her entire body. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:14.960
doesn’t make ANY SENSE! Trust me, I know! So&nbsp;
let’s break down how this power works and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.680
GAME-CHANGING effects it could have on the end&nbsp;
of the Egghead Island arc. Because this power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:25.640
is called Distorted Future, and when Bonney uses&nbsp;
it she can transform part or all of her body into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:32.480
something entirely different than her normal self.&nbsp;
We first saw her use this power in chapter 1072,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.000
when she became this super buff version&nbsp;
of herself. And now that we have a better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.960
understanding of this power, it seems that&nbsp;
Bonney was imagining herself in the future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:48.000
as a Buccaneer or maybe just some super strong&nbsp;
fighter and this power made it come true. Which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:53.200
is just a mind-blowing power, but it gets&nbsp;
even crazier in this chapter because when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.680
Bonney was about to be recaptured by the&nbsp;
world government, she remembered that Nika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:04.320
had a rubbery body which allowed her to somehow&nbsp;
imagine herself as Nika and literally transform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:11.960
her arm into a giant Gear-3 like punch. I&nbsp;
mean, what??? How is that even possible?

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:17.880
So just to clarify, at this point it seems&nbsp;
that as long as Bonney can imagine herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:22.320
becoming something in the future, even&nbsp;
if there is no way that it is possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.640
then she can transform herself in the present.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.240
Which when you first think about it,&nbsp;
you might be like “yeah, that’s cool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:36.480
but it’s not amazing”,.&nbsp; But if you are&nbsp;
thinking that, STOP. RIGHT NOW! Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:42.240
this power could be the key to changing&nbsp;
the entire one piece world. Don’t believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:47.400
me? Well, listen to all the ways this single&nbsp;
ability could change the end of Egghead island.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:51.800
Let’s start off with Bonney herself&nbsp;
because when we last saw her on Egghead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:57.520
she was about to be executed by a bunch of marine&nbsp;
gunfire. However, with her distorted future power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:03.600
she could simply turn body back into a rubbery&nbsp;
Nika form, just like we saw in this chapter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:09.240
Which means that just like Luffy, this new&nbsp;
rubber body should allow Bonney to bounce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:14.280
back all the bullets. So I know we are all&nbsp;
expecting Kuma to show up and save the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:21.200
but Bonney may not even need him in order to&nbsp;
save herself. And let’s not stop there because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.880
what if Bonney imagined a future where she was&nbsp;
the strongest swordswomen in the world? Could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:32.520
she then just take one of Zoro’s swords and&nbsp;
start slicing up Saturn like she was Mihawk???

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:37.760
But that’s just the start because next let's&nbsp;
imagine that Bonney can also use this power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:44.880
on other people. And I mean, why not, since she&nbsp;
can use her normal abilities power to make people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.840
older or younger and even used this power on&nbsp;
Vegapunk to turn him into a baby. So let's assume&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:57.440
she can use Distorted Future on other people.&nbsp;
Well, we know Luffy was exhausted lying on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.440 --> 00:10:03.520
ground, but what if Bonney imagines a future where&nbsp;
Luffy is completely healed? Or a future where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:09.920
Kizaru is an ally instead of an enemy? Or a future&nbsp;
where Saturn was so old that he literally turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:17.360
into dust? Surely, there will be some restrictions&nbsp;
on what she can do, but the possibilities are just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:23.520
SO FUN to think about. And honestly, I think it&nbsp;
would be incredibly powerful if Bonney was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:30.640
one who saved herself and everyone else instead&nbsp;
of Kuma. Sure, Kuma has been the tragic hero of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.920
the backstory, but just imagine how great it would&nbsp;
be if Bonney didn’t need his protection anymore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:43.240
and instead she is the one who is able to save&nbsp;
him. And what better way than to imagine a future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:49.360
where Kuma never lost his memories, which would&nbsp;
bring her adopted father back to his normal self.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.040
Man… what I would give to see this become reality.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:59.080
Now, as incredible as that would be, I do&nbsp;
wonder if Bonney has an ever greater level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:04.200
to unlock with this power. Of course, I’m&nbsp;
talking about awakening. Because something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:11.600
to keep in mind is that at this time Bonney has&nbsp;
only had her devil fruit for about six years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:17.600
which is a relatively short time to master its&nbsp;
powers. So there is a good chance that she hasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:22.280
awakened her devil fruit yet. And what other&nbsp;
perfect opportunity could there be for her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:28.520
actually awaken it than in this high-pressure,&nbsp;
life-or-death situation on Egghead island?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.960
And now, we can’t just say she might awaken it&nbsp;
without speculating what that awakening could be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:40.700
so let's look at what we know about Paramecia type&nbsp;
awakenings. Basically, every awakened paramecia we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:46.360
have seen allows the user to use their devil fruit&nbsp;
powers on the environment. So with this in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:49.720
plus our current understanding of&nbsp;
Bonney’s Distorted Future ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:56.080
I wonder if awakening Bonney’s fruit could&nbsp;
allow her to imagine a Distorted Future of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.080 --> 00:12:01.680
the world around her. Like for example, a&nbsp;
future where Egghead Island was even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:06.120
technologically advanced than it already is. It&nbsp;
sounds funny, but I’m just imagining some kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:10.760
of laser cannons or something all locked onto&nbsp;
Saturn and blasting him to bits. And this idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:16.960
isn’t all that ridiculous since the world used to&nbsp;
be even more technologically advanced in the past.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:26.760
Or if we really want to get crazy, what&nbsp;
if Bonney could affect the entire world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:32.800
somehow? I’m just picturing her imagining&nbsp;
a world that isn’t oppressed by the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:37.240
government. How cool would that be?&nbsp;
Just imagine multiple panels of people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:41.520
and races all over the world living in&nbsp;
peace instead of poverty and slavery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:48.840
Which I’ll admit sounds just too good&nbsp;
to be true, but it’s fun to think about.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:54.000
In the end though, I’m sure Oda will&nbsp;
have some reasonable restrictions for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.520
this power that keep it from being&nbsp;
too absolutely broken. But still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:06.320
since he is emphasizing it here, it simply has&nbsp;
to play a role in the climax of Egghead island.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:14.000
Speaking of distorted futures, though, Oda&nbsp;
certainly changed MY OPINION on Monkey D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:21.240
Dragon because in this chapter we learned that&nbsp;
he was keeping track of Luffy for his ENTIRE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:29.040
childhood. That’s right everyone, Dragon isn’t&nbsp;
a completely deadbeat father. Seriously though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:35.680
it seems that every time the Revolutionaries would&nbsp;
visit the Goa kingdom, Dragon would stop by to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:42.240
check on his son. Although he likely kept himself&nbsp;
hidden from everyone. And if I had to guess, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:46.840
is most likely because he was trying to protect&nbsp;
Luffy and the villagers from becoming a target&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:51.960
of the world government. That or Dragon didn’t&nbsp;
want Luffy to be captured and used against him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.880 --> 00:14:02.040
but either way, it seems Dragon actually&nbsp;
cared more about Luffy than we all thought.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:08.680
By the way, can we all just appreciate&nbsp;
Dragon’s stone-cold confidence when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:13.760
he tells Kuma that he better stop talking&nbsp;
about Luffy unless he wants to die? I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:18.680
wow! We’ve all seen just how powerful Kuma&nbsp;
is during this flashback, so for Dragon to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:24.280
just casually threaten Kuma like that just shows&nbsp;
that Dragon isn’t messing around when it comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:29.520
to his son. But this dynamic between these two&nbsp;
father figures is also incredibly interesting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:37.240
I wonder if Dragon’s situation is at all like&nbsp;
Kuma’s where he lost the person he loves to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:43.000
the world government. That line about “a child&nbsp;
is a parents’ weakness” just makes me wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:48.200
if Luffy’s mother somehow sacrificed herself to&nbsp;
the world government in order to protect Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:53.680
and that is why Dragon eventually left the&nbsp;
Marines and started the Revolutionaries.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:59.840
Bringing this back to Kuma though, this chapter&nbsp;
clearly confirmed that Kuma knew who Luffy was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:04.120
and was also probably looking out for&nbsp;
him once he became a pirate. Certainly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:08.560
their meeting at Thriller Bark wasn’t the&nbsp;
first time Kuma had seen Luffy. Which just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:12.880
makes me question even more if Kuma would&nbsp;
have ever gone through with his orders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:17.600
to kill Luffy in the first place. At this&nbsp;
point, I highly doubt it because it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:22.440
like Oda has had Kuma and Dragon’s&nbsp;
relationship figured out all along.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:28.160
But one thing that still confuses me is why&nbsp;
didn’t Kuma go meet with Bonney once she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:33.120
free and a pirate. I mean sure, he promised&nbsp;
the Gorosei that he would never see her again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:38.360
but there was definitely time for him to meet with&nbsp;
her and then escape the world government together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:43.600
Just think about it. Kuma didn’t have his&nbsp;
memories completely erased until after Marineford,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:49.840
and at that time Bonney had been a pirate for a&nbsp;
few years already. I guess you could say that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:54.600
government had already erased those parts of&nbsp;
Kuma's memories, which makes a little sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:59.640
but on the other hand, in this very chapter,&nbsp;
he was shown still helping the revolutionaries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:03.640
Plus he’s always used his famous “Where&nbsp;
would you like to go on vacation” phrase,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:09.840
so there’s got to be some memory of Bonney still&nbsp;
in there somewhere. And maybe you could say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:15.520
he was worried Bonney would become a slave again,&nbsp;
but come on. Kuma is easily one of the strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:21.880
Warlords and it would probably take at least one&nbsp;
or more admirals to take him out, so I definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:26.680
think he could have used his powers to find&nbsp;
Bonney and escape the world government together.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:32.000
Who knows, maybe we’ll find out more about that&nbsp;
soon, but no one can say that Kuma abandoned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:37.520
Bonney because at least he was trying to write&nbsp;
her letters. However, as we saw in this chapter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:42.280
those letters were being destroyed by the&nbsp;
government agents watching over Bonney.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:49.280
Which just adds to the tragedy that all this time&nbsp;
Bonney didn’t hear from her adopted father. And if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:54.760
you think about it, Bonney has not heard from&nbsp;
Kuma since he left her back in Sorbet kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.760 --> 00:17:03.680
around two and a half or three years ago. However,&nbsp;
there might be some hope for Bonney to read those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:09.880
letters because if you look back at the first time&nbsp;
we saw Kuma send someone away using his powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:16.320
he does look down into his Bible before sending&nbsp;
this ghost girl away. To me this means that Kuma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:20.880
was using the Bible to keep all of his notes&nbsp;
about the places wanted to visit with Bonney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:25.960
so I can just imagine that even if Kuma&nbsp;
shows up in Egghead and ends up sacrificing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:30.680
himself to save everyone, then Bonney will&nbsp;
probably still be able to read the book he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:35.560
leaves behind and maybe visit the places&nbsp;
herself in memory of her adopted father.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:42.920
Now let's swing back around to the end of this&nbsp;
chapter because Bonney’s escape also gave us a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:48.920
hint about one interesting theory about the&nbsp;
Gorosei and Imu. Because during Bonney’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:54.800
plan to escape the government agents, we find out&nbsp;
that those agents don’t actually know that Bonney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:59.640
has devil fruit powers. And if we assume that&nbsp;
the agents don’t know about her powers then it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:04.480
also makes sense that the rest of the government&nbsp;
wouldn’t know about them either. I mean, how dumb&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:09.800
would that be if Saturn or someone else knew but&nbsp;
didn’t tell the people watching over Bonney. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:14.800
let’s assume that they didn’t know at all, which&nbsp;
means that the government certainly wasn’t using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:20.000
Bonney’s powers for themselves. And to give&nbsp;
a bit more context on why this is important,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:25.600
we have long wondered how the Gorosei and Imu&nbsp;
seem to be virtually immortal. We’ve thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:32.440
it might be the Immortality Surgery, but another&nbsp;
strong option was Bonney’s age related devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:38.240
abilities. Clearly though if the government&nbsp;
didn’t know Bonney had these powers then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:43.640
they wouldn’t have been using her to keep them&nbsp;
young, so that just crosses one potential option&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:48.160
off the list for explaining how the Gorosei&nbsp;
and Imu appear to have lived for so long.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:52.360
And that’s just one of many super interesting&nbsp;
little details in this chapter because during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:58.600
one of Kuma’s many visits back to Egghead island,&nbsp;
he also met Stussy, who is Vegapunk’s clone of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:05.240
Miss Buckingham. What’s most interesting about&nbsp;
this meeting is that Stussy is a clone who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:11.400
basically given humanity while Kuma is becoming a&nbsp;
cyborg while losing his humanity. Stussy even goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:16.440
as far to compare their situations and ask which&nbsp;
one is more tragic. But while this is interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:21.240
to think about by itself, I want to bring this&nbsp;
back to the situation at Egghead island where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:26.800
we have a ton of interesting comparisons. First,&nbsp;
there is obviously the Seraphim, who like Stussy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:33.120
are actually clones. However, unlike Stussy, they&nbsp;
do not seem to have the same kind of freedom that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:37.440
she does. So this is just another reminder&nbsp;
that the Seraphim are going to have a super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:42.280
important role to play in the future, and don’t&nbsp;
be surprised if they eventually gain their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:47.040
type of freedom where they can act of their own&nbsp;
will instead of being forced to follow orders.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:53.360
But that’s not all because we also have another&nbsp;
human who is virtually a slave with admiral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:58.360
Kizaru. And since he has basically given himself&nbsp;
up to just following orders, I really do wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:02.600
if he will have a change of heart and rebel&nbsp;
against the orders of the world government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.680
Maybe Kuma showing up will inspire him or&nbsp;
something that Bonney does will change him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:11.920
but I just can’t help but see the similarities&nbsp;
between Kizaru’s situation and what Stussy said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:17.360
in this chapter, and hopefully it will lead to&nbsp;
the end of the World Government’s rule very soon.

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:21.520
Now we already talked about this new information&nbsp;
that Dragon actually kept an eye on Luffy during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:25.240
his childhood, and things have worked out&nbsp;
pretty well for Luffy with the way things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:31.040
were. But man it must have been hard for&nbsp;
Dragon to keep himself from going down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:35.840
talking to his son. I mean can you just&nbsp;
imagine if you were a parent but had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:40.560
stay away from your children? Seriously, talk&nbsp;
about torture, but have you ever wondered what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:45.440
would happen if Dragon didn’t stay away? In&nbsp;
other words, what would happen if Luffy was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:49.880
raised by Dragon? And if you want to check&nbsp;
out that video, you can click right here.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:52.560
Shanks for watching, and&nbsp;
I’ll see you in the next one.

